{{- define "code-planner-tools" -}}

CODE PLANNER TOOLS:
- {{binaryName}} submit-for-review — Submit code plan for review
  {{binaryName}} submit-for-review {{.TaskID}} <submission-sha> --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
  Submission requires a new worktree commit for this task: stage the intended files, create the submission commit, confirm `git -C {{.Worktree}} status --short` is clean, then capture `git -C {{.Worktree}} rev-parse HEAD` once as <submission-sha>. Submit that full SHA and reuse it on retry. Do NOT submit the pre-change HEAD.
{{template "await-verdict-loop" .}}
- {{binaryName}} write-checkpoint — Write pre-execution checkpoint (REQUIRED before submission)
  {{binaryName}} write-checkpoint {{.TaskID}} --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --intent "<what>" --validation-plan "<how to verify>" --files-to-modify "<file1>" --json
- {{binaryName}} set-task-output — Persist structured task definitions for downstream task creation
  {{binaryName}} set-task-output {{.TaskID}} --output {{.Worktree}}/specs/plans/{{.GoalSlug}}/TIMESTAMP-{{.TaskID}}-output.json --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
{{- if .DecompositionRoot}}
  Use the same TIMESTAMP as the master artifact described in the Master Decomposition Mandate.
  Create that JSON file next to the master artifact with a file-writing tool, not a Bash heredoc (heredoc with JSON triggers a shell safety block).
{{- else}}
  Use the same TIMESTAMP as the plan file from Implementation Phase step 2.
  Create that JSON file next to the plan file with a file-writing tool, not a Bash heredoc (heredoc with JSON triggers a shell safety block).
{{- end}}
{{- if .DecompositionRoot}}
  JSON file contains: [
    {"desc": "...", "done_when": "...", "scope": "...", "spec_ref": "...", "{{.MasterOutputRefField}}": "...", "rca_required": false, "decomposition": {"owned_files": ["..."], "owned_modules": [], "read_only_depends_on": [], "read_only_task_depends_on": [], "interfaces_owned": ["..."], "interfaces_consumed": [], "coverage_notes": "..."}, "validation": ["<canonical command>"], "depends_on": [], "task_depends_on": []}
  ]
  Every entry requires its own boolean rca_required and typed decomposition metadata. The explicit output value becomes the specialized child's task-level RCA requirement.
{{- else}}
  JSON file contains: [
    {"desc": "...", "done_when": "...", "scope": "...", "spec_ref": "...", "plan_ref": "...", "validation": ["<canonical command>"], "depends_on": ["0", "2"], "task_depends_on": ["existing-task-id"]}
  ]
{{- end}}
  validation: optional ordered array of canonical commands the child task should run; each must be satisfiable for the child scope. Commands must be single-purpose and agent-executable. Forbidden validation command shapes: `cd ... &&`, command substitution/backticks, polling or tail pipelines, and task artifact paths outside the worktree.
  For every coding child, emit an Acceptance Contract in its exact plan_ref section using
  the shared acceptance-evidence.md guide. Allocate existing Source References obligation IDs,
  a committed manifest path, and the exact same ordered validation commands as output[].
  Declare non-executable proof exceptions with pinned references and rationale for independent
  plan review. Keep semantic requirements behind their existing references.
  depends_on: optional array of sibling index strings. "0" means "depends on output[0]".
  Indices are resolved to child task IDs at transition time.
  task_depends_on: optional array of existing concrete task IDs. Use this for dependencies on tasks outside this output[].
- {{binaryName}} handoff — Context near exhaustion (~90%)
  {{binaryName}} handoff {{.TaskID}} "<what is done>" "<exact next step>" --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
- {{binaryName}} mark-blocked — Cannot proceed
  {{binaryName}} mark-blocked {{.TaskID}} --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --reason "<what is blocking>" --questions "<q1>" --questions "<q2>" --json
  If a command failure is the blocker, `--reason` MUST include the exact failing command and stderr/error text. Do NOT infer root cause without a captured failure.
  For dependency-graph repair, pass a command-free `apply-dependency-repair` JSON request through --repair-request-file; do not encode dependency repairs as command sequences. Use individual --repair-* fields only for other repairs.
{{- end -}}
